/-!
# Two-term continuous cohomology of the additive l-adic integers

Source: blueprint, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-a1-kummer/lem-exc-procyclic-two-term,
statement and proof (blueprint: lem-exc-procyclic-two-term).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace Rep

/-- Continuous cohomology of discrete modules over the additive group of l-adic integers
is computed, naturally in coefficients, by the two-term complex with differential `τ - 1`.
Here `Multiplicative` only converts the additive group to the convention of `Rep`;
`Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ℤ_[l])` is the specified additive generator, not the group identity.
The equivalences `e₀` and `e₁` identify the two nonzero terms with the coefficient module,
and their naturality equations specify the same coefficient map in both degrees.
The final natural isomorphisms identify the complex's cohomology with the recorded right
derived functors of invariants in every degree.

Proof:
1. The kernels of reduction modulo l^r give the profinite topology. Construct the functor
   K with M in degrees zero and one, differential τ - 1, and zero elsewhere. Its degree-zero
   kernel is invariants: a vector fixed by τ has an open and closed stabilizer containing
   the dense cyclic subgroup generated by τ (lem-exc-discrete-modules-abelian).
2. Underlying module exactness gives degreewise short exact sequences of K-complexes.
   The long exact homology sequence and its naturality give a cohomological delta-functor
   (lem-weil-pbc-complex-ses-homology-long-exact,
   lem-weil-pbc-complex-ses-long-exact-naturality, def-weil-pbc-delta-functor).
3. Embed M in D(M) = Cont(G,M) by m ↦ (x ↦ x • m), with translation action
   (lem-exc-coinduced-discrete-embedding). A continuous function factors through some
   G/l^rG by lem-exc-coinduced-functions-open-stabilizer and the neighbourhood basis.
4. Pull such a function back to Z/l^(r+s)Z. Its total sum is l^s times the sum on Z/l^rZ,
   hence zero. Partial sums h(a) = sum over b < a of f(b) are periodic, including the
   wraparound equation, and give a continuous h with h(x+1)-h(x) = f(x).
5. Thus τ - 1 is surjective on D(M). This embedding effaces degree one; higher degrees
   already vanish. Apply lem-weil-pbc-effaceable-delta-functor-universal to K's cohomology.
6. Continuous cochains form a delta-functor (lem-exc-continuous-cochains-delta-functor),
   effaced by the same embedding using lem-exc-coinduced-continuous-acyclic. It is universal
   by the same effaceability theorem, and its degree zero is again invariants.
7. Map continuous cochains to K by identity in degree zero, evaluation at τ in degree one,
   and zero above. The chain equation in degree zero is exactly τ • m - m; the remaining
   equations vanish. Evaluation commutes with coefficient maps.
8. By lem-exc-continuous-cochains-short-exact and naturality of the homology long exact
   sequence, this comparison induces a morphism of delta-functors, identity in degree zero.
9. Universality supplies an inverse; uniqueness makes both composites identities.
   The comparison is a quasi-isomorphism, hence an isomorphism in the ordinary derived
   category (def-weil-abstract-derived-category). The continuous-cochain description of
   def-exc-continuous-cohomology gives the stated natural cohomology isomorphisms.

Source: blueprint, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-a1-kummer/lem-exc-procyclic-two-term,
statement and all three proof paragraphs (blueprint: lem-exc-procyclic-two-term). -/
theorem exists_procyclic_twoTerm_computation
    (l : ℕ) [Fact l.Prime] (s : ℕ) (A : Type u) [Ring A] [Finite A]
    (hA : (l ^ s : ℕ) • (1 : A) = 0) :
    ∃ K : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]) ⥤
        CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{w} A) ℕ,
      ∃ (e₀ : ∀ M : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]),
          (K.obj M).X 0 ≃ₗ[A] M.obj.V)
        (e₁ : ∀ M : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]),
          (K.obj M).X 1 ≃ₗ[A] M.obj.V),
        (∀ (M N : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]))
          (f : M ⟶ N) (x : (K.obj M).X 0),
          e₀ N (((K.map f).f 0).hom x) = f.hom.hom (e₀ M x)) ∧
        (∀ (M N : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]))
          (f : M ⟶ N) (x : (K.obj M).X 1),
          e₁ N (((K.map f).f 1).hom x) = f.hom.hom (e₁ M x)) ∧
        (∀ (M : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]))
          (x : (K.obj M).X 0),
          e₁ M (((K.obj M).d 0 1).hom x) =
            M.obj.ρ (Multiplicative.ofAdd (1 : ℤ_[l])) (e₀ M x) - e₀ M x) ∧
        (∀ (M : DiscreteContinuousRep.{u, 0, w} A (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]))
          (n : ℕ), 2 ≤ n → IsZero ((K.obj M).X n)) ∧
        ∀ q : ℕ, Nonempty
          (discreteContinuousCohomologyFunctor.{0, u, w} (Multiplicative ℤ_[l]) A q ≅
            K ⋙ HomologicalComplex.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{w} A) (ComplexShape.up ℕ) q) := by
  sorry

end Rep
